B.It={sprinkles:0,glaze:1,penny:2,graham:3,cannoli:4,tira:5,barry:6}
B.U4=new A.aO("What happened to her?","Victim is Mrs. \xc9claire Senclair, founder of Senclair Confections. Somebody rolled her flat, Detective \u2014 squeezed the custard clean out of her. We traced where she fell in powdered sugar. Not a pretty sight. Barely a pastry.",null)
B.Un=new A.aO("What was the weapon?","Something long, heavy and round. A rolling pin, I'd bet a dozen on it. It's not down here \u2014 the killer carried it off and stashed it somewhere.",null)
B.x6=new A.aO("Who was in the house?","Five residents, all home, all doors locked from inside, no sign of a break-in. One of them did this \u2014 or two of them together. Could be either. Follow the crumbs, Detective.",null)
B.F_=s([B.U4,B.Un,B.x6],t.J)
B.Um=new A.aO("When did she die?","Her filling was stone cold when we got here at seven this morning. Call it around eleven last night. Find something that pins it down and I'll owe you a coffee.",null)
B.TL=new A.aO("Who found her?","The housekeeper, Penny Cotta, at half six when she came down for jam. She's been wobbling ever since. More than usual, I mean.",null)
B.TT=new A.aO("Any advice, Officer?","Search every room, talk to everyone \u2014 then talk to them again once you've got evidence to wave under their noses. People remember all sorts when you do that. When you're sure, the Chief is waiting by the front door.",null)
B.lU=s([B.Um,B.TL,B.TT],t.J)
B.x4=new A.aO("Where were you around 11 last night?","In my kitchen from half ten to half eleven, basting my Needy Souffl\xe9 every two minutes \u2014 look away and it sulks flat. At midnight I let Barry in from the greenhouse, then went to bed. I didn't go down to the cellar until morning... oh, I'm all a-wobble just thinking of it.",null)
B.TQ=new A.aO("Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Strict, but fair. She paid on time and never once called me \u201cjelly\u201d. She'd been cross with the Colonel lately, mind \u2014 something about money.",null)
B.Ui=new A.aO("Who do you suspect?","I don't like to stir the pot... but Miss Tira does love her aunt's fortune a great deal more than she loved her aunt.",null)
B.U7=new A.aO("One of your rolling pins is missing.","My marble pin! It hung right there at supper. Anyone passing through could have lifted it \u2014 I had my head in the oven from half ten. I did hear heavy footsteps behind me around quarter to eleven, mind. Marching, they were. Left, right, left, right.","rack")
B.TI=new A.aO("Who eats the ricotta in the pantry?","Eats it? Nobody eats it, Detective. That's the Colonel's filling. He springs a leak whenever he exerts himself, poor man, and I top him up on Sundays.","tub")
B.G4=s([B.x4,B.TQ,B.Ui,B.U7,B.TI],t.J)
B.Ub=new A.aO("Where were you around 11 last night?","In the parlor, playing chess with the Colonel from half past ten until midnight. I keep a scoresheet of every game, sir. It is on the chess table, should you care to inspect it.",null)
B.TS=new A.aO("Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Thirty years I served Madam. She was exacting, as a great house requires. I shall miss ironing her newspaper.",null)
B.Uq=new A.aO("Who do you suspect?","It is not a butler's place to speculate, sir. Though I will say that they always blame the butler, and I find it tiresome.",null)
B.U6=new A.aO("Your scoresheet says the Colonel left the game.","Indeed, sir. At 10:45 he announced he needed a nightcap and marched out. He returned at 11:20, quite out of breath, with no glass \u2014 and leaking a little at one end, if I may be indelicate. I spent the interval alone with the board, but I recorded the times precisely.","chess")
B.EI=s([B.Ub,B.TS,B.Uq,B.U6],t.J)
B.TK=new A.aO("Where were you around 11 last night?","In the parlor, thrashing Graham at chess! Half ten to midnight, never left my chair. A soldier holds his position, what!",null)
B.Ul=new A.aO("Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","\xc9claire? Dear old friend! Generous to a fault. We had no quarrels whatsoever. None! Why, who's been saying otherwise?",null)
B.TR=new A.aO("Who do you suspect?","That gardener, Tart. Shifty fellow, always lurking about in the boiler room. If I were hiding a weapon, that's where I'd \u2014 that's where HE'D put it, I mean.",null)
B.TX=new A.aO("Graham says you left for 35 minutes.","Ah. Yes. Well. Nightcap! Popped to the dining room for a brandy. Couldn't find the decanter. Took a while. Hardly worth mentioning, what.","chess")
B.TM=new A.aO("Is this your medal? It is made of chocolate.","I \u2014 that's \u2014 a commemorative piece! Must have dropped it weeks ago. In the boiler room, you say? I have never set foot in that boiler room in my life. Er. Except then.","medal")
B.Uc=new A.aO("You owed her 50,000 sugar cubes.","A gentleman's debts are private, sir! And she would never have told the Regiment about the medals. She... she wouldn't have had the chance. I MEAN \u2014 the heart! She wouldn't have had the heart!","ledger")
B.EJ=s([B.TK,B.Ul,B.TR,B.TX,B.TM,B.Uc],t.J)
B.U8=new A.aO("Where were you around 11 last night?","On the telephone on the landing, darling, from ten to eleven until half past. Madame Leine was describing the new spring hats in exhaustive detail. Ask the operator.",null)
B.Ud=new A.aO("Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Aunt \xc9claire was a sweet old thing with a very hard glaze. Yes, I inherit. No, I didn't flatten her for it. I look dreadful in black.",null)
B.TJ=new A.aO("Who do you suspect?","The Colonel has been jumpy as a jelly all week. He and Auntie had a screaming row in the study on Tuesday. I heard the word \u201cfraud\u201d. And \u201cfoil\u201d.",null)
B.Ua=new A.aO("The will leaves everything to you.","And it has for ten years, darling. If I were going to do it for the money, I'd hardly have sat through a decade of her bridge parties first.","will")
B.F1=s([B.U8,B.Ud,B.TJ,B.Ua],t.J)
B.x3=new A.aO("Where were you around 11 last night?","Out in the greenhouse 'til midnight, coverin' the strawberries against the frost. Penny let me in \u2014 door was latched. Left me boots on the mat like she always nags me to.",null)
B.x5=new A.aO("Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","She had a sharp tongue, but she let me sleep by the boiler when the potting shed leaks. Can't say fairer than that.",null)
B.Uk=new A.aO("Who do you suspect?","Dunno. But somethin' ain't right about that Colonel. Real soldiers don't get brown smudges on their fingers from polishin' their medals.",null)
B.U2=new A.aO("I found a rolling pin behind your boiler.","Not mine, guv! When I came in at midnight the boiler room door was hangin' open \u2014 thought Graham had been at the coal. Whoever stashed that did it before I got back. I'm a tart, not a fool.","pin")
B.Fc=s([B.x3,B.x5,B.Uk,B.U2],t.J)
B.HL=new A.bg(B.It,[B.F_,B.lU,B.G4,B.EI,B.EJ,B.F1,B.Fc],t.wU)
B.FJ=s(["graham","barry","penny","tira"],t.s)
B.Id=new A.tN("flat","The Flat Truth",B.Np,B.EC,B.HL,"Colonel Cannoli owed Mrs. Senclair 50,000 sugar cubes, and she had discovered that his medals were chocolate coins. At 10:45 he abandoned his chess game, lifted Penny's marble rolling pin from the kitchen, and at 11:05 rolled Mrs. Senclair flat in the cellar \u2014 leaking ricotta as he went. He hid the pin behind the boiler, dropped a medal in the coal, and was back at the board by 11:20, quite out of breath.",B.FJ)
B.IA={tira:0,graham:1}
B.Nl=new A.dF(B.IA,2,t.fF)
B.Jr=new A.f(565,425)
B.CD=new A.bP("urn","Overturned Espresso Urn","The huge brass urn from the pantry, emptied over the victim. It has two handles, one each side, and is far too heavy for one dessert to lift. Left handle: smeared with cocoa powder. Right handle: dusted with honey-brown cracker crumbs.","cellar",B.Jr,B.cj,B.aW)
B.IW=new A.f(330,300)
B.CG=new A.bP("stand","Empty Urn Stand","Where the espresso urn normally sits. Two sets of tracks cross the spilled flour toward the cellar: one a dainty trail dusted with cocoa, the other a row of neat, square-cornered footprints.","pantry",B.IW,B.cj,B.aW)
B.J2=new A.f(382,240)
B.Dd=new A.bI(58258,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.Bb=new A.i(1,1,0.6705882352941176,0.25098039215686274,B.d)
B.Cs=new A.bP("note","Half-Burnt Note","Fished from the furnace grate: \u201c...she signs the new will TOMORROW. It must be tonight, at eleven. I shall fetch the urn; you bring her down to the cellar. Burn this.\u201d Unsigned \u2014 but written on thick cream paper with a silver \u201cS\u201d monogram.","boiler",B.J2,B.Dd,B.Bb)
B.Cu=new A.bP("notepad","Butler's Notepad","Graham's household notepad: thick cream paper, silver \u201cS\u201d monogram. The top sheet has been torn off. Rubbing a pencil over the next page reveals the ghost of the words \u201c...must be tonight, at eleven...\u201d","dining",B.rc,B.lD,B.ej)
B.IE=new A.f(175,210)
B.CB=new A.bP("silver","Silver Cabinet","The family silver, gleaming. A tag in Penny's handwriting hangs on the door: \u201cCounted & polished \u2014 yesterday, 3 PM. All 144 pieces present.\u201d Nobody needed to count it again last night.","dining",B.IE,B.cj,B.aW)
B.Cz=new A.bP("newwill","Unsigned New Will","A draft on Mrs. Senclair's desk, due to be signed today: \u201cI revoke all bequests to my niece Tira Misu, who loves only my money. My butler, G. Cracker, is dismissed without pension for helping her pawn my pearls. Everything goes to the Donut County Home for Day-Old Pastries.\u201d","study",B.rd,B.lz,B.h)
B.Ja=new A.f(430,400)
B.Dj=new A.bI(984261,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.Cy=new A.bP("gloves","Coffee-Stained Gloves","Stuffed under Tira's mattress: a pair of elegant evening gloves, soaked through with espresso and still damp. They smell of last night.","bedroom",B.Ja,B.Dj,B.ce)
B.De=new A.bI(58305,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.Cv=new A.bP("tickets","Packed Suitcase","A suitcase hidden behind the trunks, initialled G.C. Inside: a spare butler's collar and two one-way train tickets to Biscotti Bay for tonight \u2014 \u201cMr. G. Cracker\u201d and \u201cMiss T. Misu\u201d.","storage",B.ri,B.De,B.ce)
B.CF=new A.bP("phone","Telephone Log","The operator's slip beside the attic telephone: \u201cOutgoing call, 10:50 PM \u2013 11:30 PM. Caller: Col. Cannoli. To: Fort Fondant Officers' Club.\u201d","landing",B.rj,B.lB,B.kW)
B.II=new A.f(250,395)
B.Dh=new A.bI(58671,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.Cw=new A.bP("iou","Crumpled IOU","Wedged in the Colonel's armchair: \u201cI, Col. Cannoli, owe Mrs. \xc9. Senclair 50,000 sugar cubes.\u201d A motive, certainly \u2014 but where was he at eleven?","parlor",B.II,B.Dh,B.ej)
B.EB=s([B.lp,B.lo,B.ln,B.CD,B.CG,B.Cs,B.Cu,B.CB,B.Cz,B.Cy,B.Cv,B.CF,B.Cw],t.sa)
B.Ix={sprinkles:0,glaze:1,penny:2,graham:3,tira:4,cannoli:5,barry:6}
B.U_=new A.aO("What happened to her?","Victim is Mrs. \xc9claire Senclair, founder of Senclair Confections. Somebody drenched her, Detective \u2014 gallons of scalding espresso, poured until she went soggy and simply fell apart. We outlined what was left in powdered sugar.",null)
B.TU=new A.aO("What was the weapon?","That brass espresso urn lying on its side. Thing weighs more than I do after the holidays. Take a good close look at it.",null)
B.Et=s([B.U_,B.TU,B.x6],t.J)
B.Uj=new A.aO("Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Strict, but fair. She'd been upset lately \u2014 her pearls went missing last month, and she'd been shut up with her solicitor ever since.",null)
B.U9=new A.aO("Who do you suspect?","I don't like to stir the pot... but the Colonel owes Madam a fortune. Then again, I could hear him booming down the telephone upstairs half the night, so I suppose it can't be him.",null)
B.U5=new A.aO("Was anyone counting the silver last night?","Last night? Stuff and nonsense! I counted and polished every piece at three that afternoon \u2014 it's on the tag. And the dining room is right next to my kitchen: dark and silent as a fridge from half ten onwards. Nobody was in there.","silver")
B.Fr=s([B.x4,B.Uj,B.U9,B.U5],t.J)
B.U3=new A.aO("Where were you around 11 last night?","In the dining room, sir, conducting the monthly silver inventory with Miss Tira's kind assistance. Half past ten until half past eleven. One hundred and forty-four pieces, all present.",null)
B.Uh=new A.aO("Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Thirty years I served Madam. One expects a certain... recognition, after thirty years. One does not always receive it.",null)
B.Ug=new A.aO("Who do you suspect?","The Colonel is deeply in debt to Madam, sir. And the gardener is, well, a gardener. I should look there.",null)
B.TW=new A.aO("A sheet is missing from your notepad.","A shopping list, sir. Lemons. I... burnt it. One burns shopping lists. It is a perfectly normal thing for a butler to do with lemons.","notepad")
B.TH=new A.aO("She was dismissing you without a pension.","Thirty years, sir! Thirty years of ironing newspapers, and she would have crumbled me over one string of pearls! ...Which is to say, I was unaware of any such document.","newwill")
B.Uo=new A.aO("Two tickets to Biscotti Bay, Graham?","A \u2014 a holiday, sir. Long planned. That Miss Tira's name appears on the second ticket is a clerical coincidence. I find I should like to stop answering questions now.","tickets")
B.Fo=s([B.U3,B.Uh,B.Ug,B.TW,B.TH,B.Uo],t.J)
B.TP=new A.aO("Where were you around 11 last night?","Helping Graham count the silver in the dining room, darling. Half ten to half eleven. Frightfully dull \u2014 spoons, spoons, spoons.",null)
B.TV=new A.aO("Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Auntie was a sweet old thing with a very hard glaze. We adored each other. Everyone knows I am her sole heir.",null)
B.TZ=new A.aO("Who do you suspect?","The Colonel, obviously. He owes her mountains of sugar. Or that muddy gardener. Honestly, anyone but me, darling.",null)
B.TY=new A.aO("Your gloves are soaked in espresso.","I \u2014 spilled my after-dinner coffee! All of it. On both hands. I'm a tiramisu, darling, we are practically made of coffee. It proves nothing.","gloves")
B.U1=new A.aO("Your aunt was cutting you out of her will.","She was WHAT? I mean \u2014 yes, I knew \u2014 I mean I did NOT know. Who told you I knew? Was it Graham? That crumbling old fool...","newwill")
B.G9=s([B.TP,B.TV,B.TZ,B.TY,B.U1],t.J)
B.TN=new A.aO("Where were you around 11 last night?","On the telephone on the attic landing, sir! Ten to eleven until half past, swapping war stories with old Major Meringue at the Fort Fondant Officers' Club. The operator will have a record.",null)
B.Uf=new A.aO("Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","\xc9claire? Splendid woman. Very patient with a chap's... temporary financial embarrassments.",null)
B.Up=new A.aO("Who do you suspect?","Dashed odd thing \u2014 I came downstairs past the dining room at half eleven and it was pitch dark. Yet the butler tells everyone he was counting spoons in there. Counting 'em by smell, was he?",null)
B.U0=new A.aO("You owed her 50,000 sugar cubes.","I did, and I do, and I'm not proud of it. But she'd given me until Christmas, and a dead creditor's heirs are far less patient. Her death is the worst thing that could happen to me, what!","iou")
B.Eg=s([B.TN,B.Uf,B.Up,B.U0],t.J)
B.Ue=new A.aO("Who do you suspect?","Them two \u2014 Miss Tira and old Graham \u2014 been whisperin' in corners for weeks. Go quiet as custard the moment I walk by.",null)
B.TO=new A.aO("I pulled this note out of your furnace.","Ain't my writin', guv \u2014 I can barely spell \u201cfertiliser\u201d. But when I came in at midnight the furnace door was open and the fire fresh-poked. And there was cocoa powder on the handle. I don't use cocoa. Bad for the roses.","note")
